{
  "verso": "1.1",
  "metadata": {
    "defaultKernel": "powershell",
    "activeLayout": {
      "extensionId": "verso.layout.notebook",
      "layoutId": "notebook"
    }
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "52433ee0-72cc-4894-b215-586c24679f48",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# RuleOne Financial Analysis Notebook\n\nThis notebook queries SEC EDGAR data from SQLite and visualizes financial metrics, using both F# and PowerShell in the Verso Notebook extension (see [ADR-0004](../docs/adr/ADR-0004-notebook-polyglot-language-strategy.md)):\n\n- **F#** cells query and shape the data, calling directly into the `RuleOne.ETL` and `RuleOne.Analytics` libraries.\n- **PowerShell** cells handle orchestration: rendering charts, opening files, and calling the already-built `RuleOne` PowerShell module.\n\nAll cells share one variable store, so values flow between languages without manual hand-off."
    },
    {
      "id": "af1aa2ce-4a91-49cf-8184-265cdbbad773",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "fsharp",
      "source": "// Reference the RuleOne assemblies and SQLite provider built by `dotnet build`.\n// Paths assume the notebook runs with the repository root as the working directory.\n#r \"src/RuleOne.ETL/bin/Debug/net8.0/SQLitePCLRaw.core.dll\"\n#r \"src/RuleOne.ETL/bin/Debug/net8.0/SQLitePCLRaw.provider.e_sqlite3.dll\"\n#r \"src/RuleOne.ETL/bin/Debug/net8.0/SQLitePCLRaw.batteries_v2.dll\"\n#r \"src/RuleOne.ETL/bin/Debug/net8.0/Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.dll\"\n#r \"src/RuleOne.Analytics/bin/Debug/net8.0/RuleOne.Analytics.dll\"\n#r \"src/RuleOne.ETL/bin/Debug/net8.0/RuleOne.ETL.dll\"\n\nopen RuleOne.ETL\nopen RuleOne.Analytics\n\nSQLitePCL.Batteries.Init()\n\nlet repoRoot = System.IO.Directory.GetCurrentDirectory()\nlet dbPath = System.IO.Path.Combine(repoRoot, \"ruleone.db\")\nlet connectionString = sprintf \"Data Source=%s\" dbPath\n\nprintfn \"Using database at %s\" connectionString"
    },
    {
      "id": "a22aaea0-a66f-49e4-ade0-4f82dc8caf8c",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Query Revenue and Earnings (F#)\n\nCall `RuleOne.ETL.Database.queryFactsByConcept` directly rather than re-implementing SQLite access."
    },
    {
      "id": "ba1b9799-850d-4fd6-ab6f-a2a294fd3774",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "fsharp",
      "source": "let revenueFacts = Database.queryFactsByConcept connectionString \"Revenues\"\nlet earningsFacts = Database.queryFactsByConcept connectionString \"NetIncome\"\n\nprintfn \"Found %d revenue records and %d earnings records\" revenueFacts.Length earningsFacts.Length\n\nrevenueFacts\n|> List.truncate 5\n|> List.iter (fun f ->\n    printfn \"%s - %s: $%s\"\n        (defaultArg f.CompanyName \"Unknown\")\n        (defaultArg f.Period \"Unknown\")\n        (defaultArg f.Value \"0\"))"
    },
    {
      "id": "3a8ee6ba-845c-46cc-8a86-bd4e27562605",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Shape Data and Calculate CAGR (F#)\n\nShape the raw facts into chartable records and calculate CAGR using `RuleOne.Analytics.FinancialMetrics`, leveraging F#'s records and option types."
    },
    {
      "id": "59310437-1fc2-4262-8d5d-594a583fe4e4",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "fsharp",
      "source": "type ChartPoint = { Period: string; ValueMillions: decimal }\n\nlet toMillions (value: string option) =\n    match value |> Option.bind (fun v ->\n        match System.Decimal.TryParse v with\n        | true, parsed -> Some parsed\n        | false, _ -> None) with\n    | Some parsed -> parsed / 1_000_000m\n    | None -> 0m\n\nlet revenueData =\n    revenueFacts\n    |> List.map (fun f -> { Period = defaultArg f.Period \"Unknown\"; ValueMillions = toMillions f.Value })\n    |> List.sortBy (fun r -> r.Period)\n\nlet earningsData =\n    earningsFacts\n    |> List.map (fun f -> { Period = defaultArg f.Period \"Unknown\"; ValueMillions = toMillions f.Value })\n    |> List.sortBy (fun r -> r.Period)\n\nlet revenueCagr =\n    if revenueData.Length >= 2 then\n        let first = revenueData.[0].ValueMillions\n        let last = revenueData.[revenueData.Length - 1].ValueMillions\n        let years = decimal (revenueData.Length - 1)\n        FinancialMetrics.calculateCAGR first last years\n    else\n        None\n\nmatch revenueCagr with\n| Some cagr -> printfn \"Revenue CAGR: %.2f%%\" (cagr * 100m)\n| None -> printfn \"Unable to calculate CAGR (need at least two periods of positive values)\""
    },
    {
      "id": "d9b37e06-81ce-466f-a96f-261e9ff34e5a",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualize Revenue Trend (PowerShell)\n\nRendering a chart to a file and opening it is host/OS orchestration, so this uses PowerShell. `$revenueData` was produced by the F# cells above and is available here through Verso's shared variable store."
    },
    {
      "id": "e26296b1-73b2-41cc-8e57-558a0d25dcde",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "$repoRoot = Get-Location\n$chartPath = Join-Path $repoRoot 'samples/RevenueTrend.html'\n\n$periodsJson = ($revenueData | ForEach-Object { $_.Period }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n$valuesJson = ($revenueData | ForEach-Object { $_.ValueMillions }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n\n@\"\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n    <title>Revenue Growth Trend</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-2.35.2.min.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div id=\"chart\" style=\"width:1000px;height:600px;\"></div>\n    <script>\n        Plotly.newPlot('chart', [{\n            x: $periodsJson,\n            y: $valuesJson,\n            type: 'scatter',\n            mode: 'lines+markers',\n            name: 'Revenue'\n        }], {\n            title: 'Revenue Growth Trend',\n            xaxis: { title: 'Period' },\n            yaxis: { title: 'Revenue (Millions USD)' }\n        });\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n\"@ | Set-Content -Path $chartPath -Encoding utf8\n\nInvoke-Item $chartPath\nWrite-Output \"Chart written to $chartPath\""
    },
    {
      "id": "2237f034-01da-4253-b708-65cef81643e7",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualize Revenue and Earnings Together (PowerShell)\n\nCombine `$revenueData` and `$earningsData` into one chart."
    },
    {
      "id": "d5730166-a134-4015-9286-60fac406afdd",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "$repoRoot = Get-Location\n$chartPath = Join-Path $repoRoot 'samples/RevenueAndEarningsTrend.html'\n\n$revenuePeriodsJson = ($revenueData | ForEach-Object { $_.Period }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n$revenueValuesJson = ($revenueData | ForEach-Object { $_.ValueMillions }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n$earningsPeriodsJson = ($earningsData | ForEach-Object { $_.Period }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n$earningsValuesJson = ($earningsData | ForEach-Object { $_.ValueMillions }) | ConvertTo-Json -Compress\n\n@\"\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n    <title>Revenue and Earnings Trend</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-2.35.2.min.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div id=\"chart\" style=\"width:1000px;height:600px;\"></div>\n    <script>\n        Plotly.newPlot('chart', [\n            { x: $revenuePeriodsJson, y: $revenueValuesJson, type: 'scatter', mode: 'lines+markers', name: 'Revenue' },\n            { x: $earningsPeriodsJson, y: $earningsValuesJson, type: 'scatter', mode: 'lines+markers', name: 'Net Income' }\n        ], {\n            title: 'Revenue and Earnings Trend',\n            xaxis: { title: 'Period' },\n            yaxis: { title: 'Amount (Millions USD)' }\n        });\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n\"@ | Set-Content -Path $chartPath -Encoding utf8\n\nInvoke-Item $chartPath\nWrite-Output \"Chart written to $chartPath\""
    },
    {
      "id": "48d9517c-1077-4909-b666-3abd322ba41f",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## List Securities via the RuleOne Module (PowerShell)\n\nDemonstrate the other PowerShell role from ADR-0004: calling an already-built, well-established operation \u2014 here, the `RuleOne` module's `Get-R1Securities` (see [ADR-0003](../docs/adr/ADR-0003-powershell-module-design.md)) \u2014 instead of writing new query logic."
    },
    {
      "id": "07b55562-8b8a-476c-97ac-ee2c0d94f386",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "powershell",
      "source": "Import-Module (Join-Path (Get-Location) 'modules/RuleOne/RuleOne.psd1') -Force\n\nGet-R1Securities | Format-Table -AutoSize"
    },
    {
      "id": "c1886910-1cbd-48b5-a9a6-6804caf8f884",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Summary\n\nThis notebook demonstrates:\n- Querying financial facts (revenue, earnings) directly through `RuleOne.ETL.Database` in F#\n- Shaping data and calculating CAGR through `RuleOne.Analytics` in F#\n- Visualizing trends using Plotly (rendered as standalone HTML, opened in your browser) in PowerShell\n- Orchestrating an already-built operation (`Get-R1Securities`) through the `RuleOne` PowerShell module\n\nTo use this notebook:\n1. Build the solution so the referenced assemblies exist: `dotnet build`\n2. Fetch some data: `dotnet run --project src/RuleOne.ETL 0000789019 10-K`\n3. Install the [Verso Notebook](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=Datafication.verso-notebook) extension and open this file with it\n4. Execute cells sequentially from the repository root"
    }
  ]
}
